## Update these instructions after a reviewed GitHub sync

The editable, Git-tracked sources for this workspace are `../github/infrastructure/codex_workspace/*.template`. These local copies are deployed by a hash-guarded installer:

```bash
# Run only while the checkout and workspace have no other writer.
(cd ../github && bash scripts/sync_main.sh)  # clean, idle main only
.venv/bin/python ../github/scripts/install_codex_workspace.py --check
.venv/bin/python ../github/scripts/install_codex_workspace.py
```

The installer refuses locally edited or unknown files rather than discarding them. Edit the tracked templates for permanent changes; preserve/reconcile intentional local edits before refreshing. It does not touch `.venv`, datasets, checkpoints, source symlinks, credentials, or scientific code.

## Data safety

Ignored local data/results are not backed up by GitHub. Never delete them while syncing. Do not use `git clean`, `git reset --hard`, automatic stashing, directory replacement, or force pushes. Use fixed-commit execution worktrees for approved long runs and a separate backup target for irreplaceable outputs. Do not pull or switch branches in a checkout used by a running experiment.
